WEBVTT

00:00:00.537 --> 00:00:03.310
Telemetry signals answer different operational questions.

00:00:03.310 --> 00:00:05.565
Metrics summarize numeric behavior over time.

00:00:05.565 --> 00:00:09.277
They are useful for latency, error rate, throughput, request volume, queue depth,

00:00:09.277 --> 00:00:12.280
GPU utilization, memory pressure, and similar trends.

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:14.200
Metrics are compact and easy to alert on,

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:17.190
but they usually do not explain the full story by themselves.

00:00:17.190 --> 00:00:19.310
Logs record discrete events and details.

00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:23.840
A log entry can explain that a route selected a model version, a retrieval call timed out,

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:27.200
a pipeline job skipped a source, or an administrative change occurred.

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:31.140
Logs are valuable during investigation, but they need structure and data discipline.

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:34.925
They should provide useful context without turning sensitive request content into

00:00:34.925 --> 00:00:35.710
permanent records.

00:00:35.710 --> 00:00:37.600
Traces connect work across services.

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:39.099
In a distributed AI workflow,

00:00:39.099 --> 00:00:43.110
a trace can show that a request moved from an API gateway to an inference service,

00:00:43.110 --> 00:00:45.660
then to retrieval, storage, and a downstream service.

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:50.285
Traces help teams distinguish time spent in application logic from time spent waiting on

00:00:50.285 --> 00:00:50.790
dependencies,

00:00:50.790 --> 00:00:52.300
scheduling, or network calls.

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:56.025
Events and audit records capture important state changes, policy decisions,

00:00:56.025 --> 00:00:58.870
administrative actions, and security-relevant activity.

00:00:58.870 --> 00:01:02.795
Profiles and health checks add another view by showing performance characteristics and

00:01:02.795 --> 00:01:03.380
readiness.

00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:04.620
No single signal is enough.

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:09.140
A useful operating picture combines metrics for trends, logs for detail, traces for flow,

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:13.680
events for change, audits for accountability, and health checks for current state.
